  "ingredients": [
    "816 gram boneless, skinless chicken breast",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "1 cup mozzarella cheese (shredded)",
    "2 1/2 ounce pork rinds",
    "1/4 cup flaxseed meal",
    "1/2 cup parmesan cheese (shredded)",
    "2 teaspoon paprika",
    "1 teaspoon dried oregano",
    "1/2 teaspoon salt",
    "1/2 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1/2 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes",
    "1 large egg",
    "1 1/2 teaspoon chicken broth",
    "1/4 cup olive oil",
    "1 cup low-carb tomato sauce (such as Rao's)",
    "1/4 cup olive oil",
    "1/2 teaspoon fresh garlic",
    "1/2 teaspoon dried oregano",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 400F. In a food processor, grind up the pork rinds, flaxseed meal, parmesan cheese, and spices. Transfer the mixture to a shallow bowl.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/simple-chicken-parmesan/#wprm-recipe-51471-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_7773.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the chicken breasts in half and pound them out into cutlets. Season with salt and pepper to taste.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/simple-chicken-parmesan/#wprm-recipe-51471-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_7789.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate shallow bowl from the coating, whisk the egg together with the chicken broth.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/simple-chicken-parmesan/#wprm-recipe-51471-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_7796.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a saucepan over medium heat, whisk together all of the ingredients for the sauce. Let this cook for at least 20 minutes while preparing the chicken.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/simple-chicken-parmesan/#wprm-recipe-51471-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_7799.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bread the chicken cutlets by dipping them in the egg mixture and then dipping them in the coating mixture. Set the breaded cutlets aside on a piece of foil.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/simple-chicken-parmesan/#wprm-recipe-51471-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_7811.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat about half of the olive oil in a pan and fry each piece of chicken on both sides until crispy, adding more oil as needed. Fry the chicken in batches, so as not to overcrowd the pan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/simple-chicken-parmesan/#wprm-recipe-51471-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_7825.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the chicken in a casserole dish, pour the sauce over the top, and sprinkle with the mozzarella cheese. Bake for 10 minutes, or until the cheese is nice and melted.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/simple-chicken-parmesan/#wprm-recipe-51471-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/img_7843.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve with side of choice. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/simple-chicken-parmesan/#wprm-recipe-51471-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
